---

---

<section id="faq" class="py-[var(--row)] border-b border-rule">
  <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-[var(--gutter)]">
    <header class="mb-9">
      <pre
        class="font-mono text-[clamp(10px,1.1vw,13px)] leading-[1.1] text-ink mb-[18px]"><span class="hi">## 05 ─</span> frequently asked ───────────────────────────────────────────</pre>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-ink2 max-w-[70ch] m-0">
        Questions no one asked, but I'm answering anyway.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="border-t border-b border-rule">
      <details open class="border-b border-dashed border-rule-soft">
        <summary
          class="cursor-pointer grid grid-cols-[70px_1fr_30px] gap-[18px] items-center p-[16px_18px] hover:bg-bg2 max-[720px]:grid-cols-[50px_1fr_24px]"
        >
          <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.10em] text-ink3"
            >Q.01</span
          >
          <span
            class="text-[15px] leading-[1.35] text-ink font-medium tracking-[-0.005em]"
            >is this <em class="not-italic text-accent">production</em
            >-ready?</span
          >
          <span class="faq-toggle text-right text-ink3 text-sm font-semibold"
          ></span>
        </summary>
        <p
          class="m-0 p-[0_18px_18px_106px] text-ink2 text-[13px] leading-[1.65] max-w-[80ch] max-[720px]:pl-[78px]"
        >
          No. Not even close. It's not mature enough to be considered a toy
          database, let alone a production one. If you're asking this seriously,
          I'm concerned.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-dashed border-rule-soft">
        <summary
          class="cursor-pointer grid grid-cols-[70px_1fr_30px] gap-[18px] items-center p-[16px_18px] hover:bg-bg2 max-[720px]:grid-cols-[50px_1fr_24px]"
        >
          <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.10em] text-ink3"
            >Q.05</span
          >
          <span
            class="text-[15px] leading-[1.35] text-ink font-medium tracking-[-0.005em]"
            >why <em class="not-italic text-accent">zig</em>?</span
          >
          <span class="faq-toggle text-right text-ink3 text-sm font-semibold"
          ></span>
        </summary>
        <p
          class="m-0 p-[0_18px_18px_106px] text-ink2 text-[13px] leading-[1.65] max-w-[80ch] max-[720px]:pl-[78px]"
        >
          I just wanted to learn Zig. No grand vision, no benchmark slides.
          Just vibes.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary
          class="cursor-pointer grid grid-cols-[70px_1fr_30px] gap-[18px] items-center p-[16px_18px] hover:bg-bg2 max-[720px]:grid-cols-[50px_1fr_24px]"
        >
          <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.10em] text-ink3"
            >Q.03</span
          >
          <span
            class="text-[15px] leading-[1.35] text-ink font-medium tracking-[-0.005em]"
            >how do i contribute?</span
          >
          <span class="faq-toggle text-right text-ink3 text-sm font-semibold"
          ></span>
        </summary>
        <p
          class="m-0 p-[0_18px_18px_106px] text-ink2 text-[13px] leading-[1.65] max-w-[80ch] max-[720px]:pl-[78px]"
        >
          I'm not accepting contributions right now — that would defeat the
          whole point of a learning project.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary
          class="cursor-pointer grid grid-cols-[70px_1fr_30px] gap-[18px] items-center p-[16px_18px] hover:bg-bg2 max-[720px]:grid-cols-[50px_1fr_24px]"
        >
          <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.10em] text-ink3"
            >Q.04</span
          >
          <span
            class="text-[15px] leading-[1.35] text-ink font-medium tracking-[-0.005em]"
            >do you use AI?</span
          >
          <span class="faq-toggle text-right text-ink3 text-sm font-semibold"
          ></span>
        </summary>
        <p
          class="m-0 p-[0_18px_18px_106px] text-ink2 text-[13px] leading-[1.65] max-w-[80ch] max-[720px]:pl-[78px]"
        >
          Yes, a lot — but I try not to let it just write everything for me. I
          slow down, read the output, understand it, and rewrite it myself when
          I can. Muscle memory in Zig won't build itself.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
